<# Selected publications for the one-pager. EMPTY by default — the untailored CV shows counts
   (\journalpapers etc.) rather than a list, and the page has no room for both. An application
   manifest selects 3-5 bib keys; the entries themselves come from cv/publications.bib, so the
   only tailoring lever here is WHICH, never WHAT.

   Titles/venues are .bib-derived, not LaTeX, so they go through `texesc`.

   The \vspace{\topsep} is load-bearing. \section has zero after-space in the class and
   tightemize opens with \vspace{-\topsep}, so without it the first item is pulled up into the
   heading and the two overprint. Experience never shows this because a \runsubsection line
   always sits between its heading and its list. #>
<% if publications.length %>
\section{Selected Publications}
\vspace{\topsep}
\begin{tightemize}
<% for p in publications %>
    \item << p.title | texesc >><% if p.venue %> --- \textit{<< p.venue | texesc >>}<% endif %><% if p.year %>, << p.year >><% endif %>.
<% endfor %>
\end{tightemize}
\sectionsep
<% endif %>
